shape theory.chemistry.bio.replication : theory.chemistry.bio.cell, theory.chemistry.bio.genetic-code, theory.branching {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Replication, Mutation, and Selection as Canopy Dynamics.
//
// DNA replication is the molecular implementation of the
// transformation law: M' = f(C, S) where the template strand
// (C) and DNA polymerase (S) produce a new strand (M').
//
// Replication fidelity:
//   DNA polymerase error rate: ~10^-8 per base per replication.
//   The polymerase has proofreading (3'->5' exonuclease):
//   it checks its own output and corrects errors.
//   This is active coherence maintenance (Theorem 11.10):
//   the system continuously resolves incoherence.
//
// Mutation as branching:
//   Errors that escape proofreading are mutations: changes to
//   the structure S itself. This is structural change
//   (Definition 16.5). Most mutations are neutral (the canopy
//   center is broad) or harmful (moving away from coherence).
//   Rarely, a mutation increases coherence in the current
//   environment: the organism is more fit.
//
// Natural selection as coherence filtering:
//   Organisms that cohere in their environment persist.
//   Organisms that don't, dissolve (die, fail to reproduce).
//   This IS Law 0: what persists must cohere.
//   Selection is not an external force acting on organisms.
//   It is coherence itself, operating at the organismal level.
//   The environment is the context; the organism is the shape;
//   persistence requires coherence with context.
//
// The canopy of life:
//   Every coherent genome persists (Landscape Completeness at
//   the biological level). The diversity of life is the canopy
//   of genomic structure: all coherent traces through the space
//   of possible genomes, weighted by structural probability
//   (fitness = structural weight in the environmental context).
//
// Evolution is the moment sequence of the biosphere:
//   M -> M' -> M'' -> ... where each M is the current state
//   of all organisms, and the transformation is replication +
//   mutation + selection + drift. The biosphere is a shape
//   that transforms while maintaining continuity. Evolution
//   IS persistence at the species level.
//
// Derives from: theory.chemistry.bio.cell,
//               theory.chemistry.bio.genetic-code,
//               theory.branching (branch points, traces, canopy)
  """
}
